                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's great work done by one man, but unfortunately it's also the reason I don't recommend the game.\nI played it for 16 mins. and have already seen all it has to offer. €9,99 is just waaay to high for that amount of playtime.\nNext... the game was released... and then the guy clearly went off to do something else. The game has some clear usability issues that could have been discovered via player testing, and there are tons of ways the game could have small improvements.... but the developer is gone.\n\nIt's a four level wave shooter, and the levels are ok.\nWhat breaks the game is a terrible reload mechanic. Throw away your gun and grab a new one... sounds good, but works terrible. It's almost like pressing the grip-buttons twice should do the job, but it does not really.\n\nThe movement mechanic. is also terrible. It requires you to shoot at specific targets, and then moves to to that place. Sounds fine, but...  Since the reloads are terrible, and you need ammo to move, this leads to problems.  Also, sometimes in a gunfights you hit those targets and move when you did not intend to.\n\nBoth could be fixed easily: Reloads could be done like EVERY ONE ELSE, by simply pointing the guns downward. It works, why do it different?\n\nMovement could then be switched to the grip buttons or something, which would fix the other problem.\n\ntl;dr; Great graphics, poor gameplay.",
